   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>טוב עם קצת עזרה ממי שכתב את החבילה הצלחתי לפתור את העניין:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\">The issue is due to an escape character in one of the strings &quot;\\b&quot;</div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><div>&gt; x &lt;- read.csv(&quot;file1.txt&quot;)</div><div>&gt; x[150,44]</div><div>[1] ÷øéîéðåìåâéä áäúîçåú áîãò ôåøðæé - îåñîê   <b> \\b</b></div><div><b><br></b></div><div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">To work around this issue:</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">x &lt;- read.csv(&quot;file1.txt&quot;, stringsAsFactors = FALSE)</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">wb &lt;- createWorkbook()</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">addWorksheet(wb, &quot;Sheet 1&quot;)</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">is_character_col &lt;- which(sapply(x, class) %in% &quot;character&quot;)</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">for(i in is_character_col){</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">  x[[i]] &lt;- gsub(&quot;\\b&quot;, &quot;&quot;, x[[i]], fixed = TRUE)</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">}</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">  </div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">writeDataTable(wb, 1, x)</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">saveWorkbook(wb, &quot;hopefully_fixed.xlsx&quot;)</div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>On Wednesday, January 13, 2016 at 3:31:25 PM UTC+2, eliav schmulewitz wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">sorry in advance for the cross posting i posted this on stack overflow, but i think that because this involves a problem with Hebrew i should post here as well :<div><a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/34763526/write-xlsx-with-openxlsx-package-for-large-data-frames-that-include-utf-8-charac\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/34763526/write-xlsx-with-openxlsx-package-for-large-data-frames-that-include-utf-8-charac&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496987745000&amp;usg=AOvVaw02Bm95sFFCbUsNTVU2rXhx\">this is the SO link</a></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;color:rgb(34,36,38);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:16.9px\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"padding-right:15px;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"text-align:center;min-width:46px\"><span style=\"margin-top:8px;margin-bottom:8px;font-size:20px;display:block;color:rgb(119,119,119)\"><br></span><a title=\"This question does not show any research effort; it is unclear or not useful\" style=\"margin-right:auto;margin-bottom:10px;margin-left:auto;font-size:1px;color:rgb(0,119,204);overflow:hidden;display:block;width:40px;min-height:30px;background-image:url(&quot;&quot;),none;background-position:0px -220px;background-repeat:no-repeat\" rel=\"nofollow\">down vote</a><a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/34763526/write-xlsx-with-openxlsx-package-for-large-data-frames-that-include-utf-8-charac#\" title=\"This is a favorite question (click again to undo)\" style=\"margin-right:auto;margin-bottom:2px;margin-left:auto;font-size:1px;color:rgb(0,119,204);overflow:hidden;display:block;width:40px;min-height:30px;background-image:url(&quot;&quot;),none;background-position:0px -120px;background-repeat:no-repeat\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/34763526/write-xlsx-with-openxlsx-package-for-large-data-frames-that-include-utf-8-charac%23&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496987745000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0pyXBfoDuBAA791fUJjq5G\">favorite</a><div><span style=\"color:rgb(119,119,119)\"></span></div></div></td><td style=\"vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;font-size:15px;width:660px;word-wrap:break-word;line-height:1.3\"><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;clear:both\">I am trying to write a fairly large data frame (more than 200 columns and more than 6000 rows) that includes Hebrew characters to excel using the openxlsx package through shiny.<br>For some reason when I download the file I get a corrupt excel file, when trying to open it i get a</p><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 10px;padding:10px;border-width:0px 0px 0px 2px;border-left-style:solid;border-left-color:rgb(255,235,142);quotes:none;background-color:rgb(255,248,220)\"><p style=\"clear:both\">excel found unreadable content do you want to recover the contents of this workbook</p></blockquote><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;clear:both\">and then:</p><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 10px;padding:10px;border-width:0px 0px 0px 2px;border-left-style:solid;border-left-color:rgb(255,235,142);quotes:none;background-color:rgb(255,248,220)\"><p style=\"clear:both\">excel was able to open the file by repairing or removing the unreadable content</p></blockquote><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;clear:both\">Once i open the file all the hebrew characters are gone!<br>Trying to reproduce this issue I found that if I try writing a smaller data frame for instance [100:100] it works the hebrew is there, but once i make my data frame larger it does not work.<br><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0Bzhw9flL8QdsQTlVeGhTSXh4Yms/view?usp=sharing\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(0,89,153)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://drive.google.com/file/d/0Bzhw9flL8QdsQTlVeGhTSXh4Yms/view?usp%3Dsharing&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496987745000&amp;usg=AOvVaw37mL6IWjXVvKbPOUonz1hI\">Here</a> is a link to the file I am using in the test code below <br>and here is the code i am using: <br><strong>server.R</strong></p><pre style=\"margin-bottom:1em;padding:5px;font-size:13px;overflow:auto;width:auto;max-height:600px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;color:rgb(57,51,24);word-wrap:normal;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\"><code style=\"font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:inherit\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">library</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">shiny</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n    library</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">openxlsx</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n    shinyServer</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,139)\">function</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">input</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> output</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">{</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n      datasetInput </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> reactive</span><span s